SI No,Test Case Name,Test Case Description,IP Name,Test Folder Path,Source File,Register Name,Register Offset,Register Width,Register Field Name,Register Field Index,Register Field Type,Reset Value,Register Description,Register Token (Address Macro),Register Token (Default Value),Register Token (Read Mask),Register Token (Write Mask),Test Type,Test Methodology,Preconditions,Test Steps,Expected Result,Pass/Fail Criteria,Priority,Coverage Area,Applicable GPIO Pins,Notes
1,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test verifies the default reset values of GPIO per-pin registers (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10) after system reset. Each register is read and its value is masked with 0xFFFFFFFE (bit 0 excluded as data_in is externally driven) and compared against the expected default value from the specification.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_gpio_8,0x0,32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Determines the level gpio pin; Interrupt raw status; Writing 1 clears the interrupt raw status; Pos-edge interrupt enable; Neg-edge interrupt enable; GPIO Pin signal level select; GPIO mode select: 0-output 1-input; GPIO output data",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK,Default Value Check,Polling,System reset must be completed before test execution. GPIO IP must be out of reset.,"1. Perform system reset to bring all GPIO registers to their default state.
2. Read the gp0_gpio_8 register.
3. Mask the read value with 0xFFFFFFFE to exclude the externally-driven data_in bit.
4. Compare the masked value against the expected default value from the register specification.
5. Repeat steps 2-4 for gp0_gpio_9 and gp0_gpio_10.
6. Report PASS if all registers match their expected default values; otherwise report FAIL.",All GPIO per-pin registers read back their expected default values after reset with bit 0 masked out.,PASS: All registers match expected default values after masking with 0xFFFFFFFE. FAIL: Any register default value mismatch detected (def_fail_cnt > 0).,High,Register Default Value Verification,"GPIO pins 8, 9, 10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Bit 0 (data_in) is excluded from comparison using mask 0xFFFFFFFE because it reflects the external pin level which is not deterministic after reset. Registers with skip_rst_array=1 or read_mask=0x00000000 are skipped."
2,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test verifies the default reset value of gp0_gpio_9 register after system reset. The register is read, masked with 0xFFFFFFFE, and compared against the expected default value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_gpio_9,0x4,32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Determines the level gpio pin; Interrupt raw status; Writing 1 clears the interrupt raw status; Pos-edge interrupt enable; Neg-edge interrupt enable; GPIO Pin signal level select; GPIO mode select; GPIO output data",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK,Default Value Check,Polling,System reset must be completed. GPIO IP must be out of reset.,"1. Perform system reset.
2. Read the gp0_gpio_9 register.
3. Mask the read value with 0xFFFFFFFE.
4. Compare against the expected default value.
5. Report PASS if matched; FAIL otherwise.",The gp0_gpio_9 register reads back its expected default value after reset with bit 0 masked out.,PASS: Register matches expected default value. FAIL: Default value mismatch detected.,High,Register Default Value Verification,GPIO pin 9 (gp0_gpio_9),Bit 0 (data_in) excluded from comparison. Registers with skip_rst_array=1 are skipped.
3,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test verifies the default reset value of gp0_gpio_10 register after system reset. The register is read, masked with 0xFFFFFFFE, and compared against the expected default value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_gpio_10,0x8,32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Determines the level gpio pin; Interrupt raw status; Writing 1 clears the interrupt raw status; Pos-edge interrupt enable; Neg-edge interrupt enable; GPIO Pin signal level select; GPIO mode select; GPIO output data",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK,GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK,Default Value Check,Polling,System reset must be completed. GPIO IP must be out of reset.,"1. Perform system reset.
2. Read the gp0_gpio_10 register.
3. Mask the read value with 0xFFFFFFFE.
4. Compare against the expected default value.
5. Report PASS if matched; FAIL otherwise.",The gp0_gpio_10 register reads back its expected default value after reset with bit 0 masked out.,PASS: Register matches expected default value. FAIL: Default value mismatch detected.,High,Register Default Value Verification,GPIO pin 10 (gp0_gpio_10),Bit 0 (data_in) excluded from comparison. Registers with skip_rst_array=1 are skipped.
4,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0xFFFFFFFF to all writable GPIO per-pin registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10) masked with each register's write mask, then reads back each register masked with the read mask and compares against the expected value computed as: (pattern & read_mask & write_mask) | (~write_mask & read_mask & default_value).",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Default value check completed. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0xFFFFFFFF masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back with appropriate masking.,PASS: Read-back value matches expected computed value for all registers. FAIL: Any write-read mismatch detected (wr_fail_cnt > 0).,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Registers with skip_array[i]=1 are skipped (VRRW registers at offsets 0x80, 0x94-0xB0). Write-only fields (intr_clr) are not read back. Read-only fields (data_in, intr_raw_sts) retain their hardware-driven values."
5,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0xAAAAAAAA to all writable GPIO per-pin registers masked with each register's write mask, then reads back and verifies against the expected computed value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0xAAAAAAAA masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back.,PASS: Read-back matches expected value. FAIL: Any mismatch detected.,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Pattern 0xAAAAAAAA tests alternating bit pattern (1010...). VRRW registers skipped."
6,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0x55555555 to all writable GPIO per-pin registers masked with each register's write mask, then reads back and verifies against the expected computed value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0x55555555 masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back.,PASS: Read-back matches expected value. FAIL: Any mismatch detected.,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Pattern 0x55555555 tests complementary alternating bit pattern (0101...). VRRW registers skipped."
7,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0xF5F5F5F5 to all writable GPIO per-pin registers masked with each register's write mask, then reads back and verifies against the expected computed value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0xF5F5F5F5 masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back.,PASS: Read-back matches expected value. FAIL: Any mismatch detected.,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Pattern 0xF5F5F5F5 tests mixed nibble pattern. VRRW registers skipped."
8,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0xA5A5A5A5 to all writable GPIO per-pin registers masked with each register's write mask, then reads back and verifies against the expected computed value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0xA5A5A5A5 masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back.,PASS: Read-back matches expected value. FAIL: Any mismatch detected.,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Pattern 0xA5A5A5A5 tests another mixed nibble pattern. VRRW registers skipped."
9,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"This test writes the pattern 0xFFFF0000 to all writable GPIO per-pin registers masked with each register's write mask, then reads back and verifies against the expected computed value.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10","0x0; 0x4; 0x8",32,"data_in; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; pedge_intr_en; nedge_intr_en; level_sel; io_ctrl; dout","0; 1; 16; 17; 18; 19; 20; 21","RO; RO; WO; RW; RW; RW; RW2; RW2","0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 1; 0","Per-pin GPIO control register fields","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_DEFAULT_VAL","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_READ_MASK","GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9_WRITE_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10_WRITE_MASK",Write-Read Test,Polling,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. Registers with skip_array=1 or write_mask=0x00000000 are skipped.","1. Write the pattern 0xFFFF0000 masked with the write mask to each writable GPIO per-pin register.
2. Read back each register and mask the result with the read mask.
3. Compute the expected value considering writable and non-writable bits.
4. Compare the read-back value against the expected value.
5. Report PASS if all registers match; FAIL otherwise.",All writable GPIO registers retain the expected bit pattern after write and read-back.,PASS: Read-back matches expected value. FAIL: Any mismatch detected.,High,Register Write-Read Verification,"GPIO pins 8-10 (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_10)","Pattern 0xFFFF0000 tests upper-half/lower-half boundary. VRRW registers skipped."
10,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies GPIO level-select interrupt functionality in active-high mode for all 32 GPIO pins (GPIO 8 through GPIO 39). Each GPIO pin is configured in input mode with level_sel=1 (active-high), the group interrupt is enabled, an external stimulus is applied via SRAM write, and the ISR validates that the interrupt is raised, the raw status bit is set, the group interrupt status reflects the correct pin, the interrupt is successfully cleared, and the sysreg interrupt status is cleared.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_intr1_intr_en1; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1; raw_stcr1; intr_en1","0x0; 0x84; 0x88; 0x24; 0x28",32,"level_sel; io_ctrl; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; gpio0_intr","19; 20; 1; 16; 1","RW; RW2; RO; WO; RAWSTCR1","0; 1; 0; 0; 0","GPIO level select for interrupt polarity; GPIO input/output mode control; Interrupt raw status; Interrupt clear; GPIO0 interrupt status in sysreg","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1",NA,NA,NA,Interrupt Functional - Active High Level,ISR,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. GIC must be initialized. IRQ 87 (for GPIO0) must be enabled. Sysreg interrupt for GPIO0 must be enabled.","1. Enable GIC IRQ for GPIO0 interrupt line.
2. Enable the GPIO0 interrupt in the sysreg interrupt enable register (intr_en1).
3. For each GPIO pin (0 to 31): configure the corresponding per-pin register in input mode with level_sel=1 (active-high interrupt).
4. Enable the group interrupt for the current pin in the group interrupt enable register (gp0_intr1_intr_en1).
5. Write a stimulus value to the external SRAM location to trigger the interrupt.
6. Wait for the ISR to fire and validate: (a) interrupt raw status bit is set in the per-pin register, (b) group interrupt status register reflects the correct pin, (c) interrupt is cleared by writing to the intr_clr field, (d) read-back confirms interrupt cleared (expected value 0x100001), (e) group interrupt status is 0 after disabling group enable, (f) sysreg raw status is cleared.
7. Clear the GIC IRQ after ISR processing.
8. Report PASS if all 32 pins pass all checks; FAIL if any test_err increments.",All 32 GPIO pins generate level-triggered interrupts in active-high mode. Interrupt raw status is correctly set and cleared. Group interrupt status reflects the correct pin. Sysreg interrupt status is properly cleared.,"PASS: All 32 GPIO pins pass interrupt raise, status check, clear, group status clear, and sysreg clear validations (test_err == 0). FAIL: Any pin fails any validation step (test_err > 0).",High,Interrupt Functional Verification - Active High Level,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"Requires GIC initialization and IRQ 87 enabled for GPIO0 instance. The SRAM address 0xA0243ffc is used as an external stimulus trigger. The int_pend flag is used for ISR synchronization. Active-high means level_sel bit (bit 19) is set to 1."
11,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies GPIO level-select interrupt functionality in active-low mode for all 32 GPIO pins (GPIO 8 through GPIO 39). Each GPIO pin is configured in input mode with level_sel=0 (active-low), the group interrupt is enabled, an inverted stimulus pattern is applied via SRAM write, and the ISR validates interrupt raise, status, clear, and sysreg clear.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c","gp0_gpio_8; gp0_intr1_intr_en1; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1; raw_stcr1; intr_en1","0x0; 0x84; 0x88; 0x24; 0x28",32,"level_sel; io_ctrl; intr_raw_sts; intr_clr; gpio0_intr","19; 20; 1; 16; 1","RW; RW2; RO; WO; RAWSTCR1","0; 1; 0; 0; 0","GPIO level select for interrupt polarity; GPIO input/output mode control; Interrupt raw status; Interrupt clear; GPIO0 interrupt status in sysreg","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1",NA,NA,NA,Interrupt Functional - Active Low Level,ISR,"System reset completed. GPIO IP out of reset. GIC must be initialized. IRQ 87 (for GPIO0) must be enabled. Sysreg interrupt for GPIO0 must be enabled.","1. Enable GIC IRQ for GPIO0 interrupt line.
2. Enable the GPIO0 interrupt in the sysreg interrupt enable register (intr_en1).
3. For each GPIO pin (0 to 31): configure the corresponding per-pin register in input mode with level_sel=0 (active-low interrupt).
4. Enable the group interrupt for the current pin in the group interrupt enable register (gp0_intr1_intr_en1).
5. Write an inverted stimulus value (~(1<<pin)) to the external SRAM location to trigger the active-low interrupt.
6. Wait for the ISR to fire and validate: (a) interrupt raw status bit is set, (b) group interrupt status reflects the correct pin, (c) interrupt is cleared successfully, (d) group interrupt status is 0 after disabling, (e) sysreg raw status is cleared.
7. Clear the GIC IRQ after ISR processing.
8. Report PASS if all 32 pins pass; FAIL if any test_err increments.",All 32 GPIO pins generate level-triggered interrupts in active-low mode. All interrupt status and clear validations pass.,"PASS: All 32 GPIO pins pass all active-low interrupt validations (test_err == 0). FAIL: Any pin fails any validation step (test_err > 0).",High,Interrupt Functional Verification - Active Low Level,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"Requires GIC initialization and IRQ 87 enabled for GPIO0 instance. Active-low means level_sel bit (bit 19) is set to 0. The SRAM stimulus uses inverted bit pattern ~(1<<i) to drive the pin low for the target GPIO."
12,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the GPIO group interrupt enable and disable mechanism via the gp0_intr1_intr_en1 register. The test enables individual pin interrupts by writing (1<<i) to the group enable register and later disables by writing 0x00000000, then verifies the group interrupt status register reads 0x0 after disable.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_intr1_intr_en1,0x84,32,G8_intr_en through G39_intr_en,0-31,RW,0,"Group interrupt enable bits for GPIO pins 8-39, one bit per pin",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1,NA,NA,NA,Interrupt Enable/Disable Verification,ISR,"GPIO IP out of reset. Per-pin interrupt must be configured before enabling group interrupt.","1. Write the bit mask (1<<pin) to the group interrupt enable register to enable interrupt for a specific GPIO pin.
2. Trigger the interrupt via external stimulus.
3. In the ISR, write 0x00000000 to the group interrupt enable register to disable all group interrupts.
4. Read the group interrupt status register and verify it returns 0x0.
5. Repeat for all 32 GPIO pins.
6. Report PASS if group status is always 0 after disable; FAIL otherwise.",Group interrupt status register reads 0x0 after group interrupt enable register is written with 0x00000000.,"PASS: gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 == 0x0 after disabling group interrupt enable. FAIL: gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 != 0x0 (group interrupt clear failed).",High,Interrupt Group Enable/Disable,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"Group interrupt enable register controls which pin interrupts propagate to the group status. Writing 0x00000000 disables all pin interrupts at the group level."
13,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the GPIO group interrupt status register (gp0_intr1_intr_sts1) correctly reflects the interrupting pin. When a pin interrupt fires, the corresponding bit in the group status register should be set. After clearing, the status should return to 0x0.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_intr1_intr_sts1,0x88,32,G8_intr_sts through G39_intr_sts,0-31,RO,0,"Group interrupt status bits for GPIO pins 8-39, one bit per pin (read-only)",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1,NA,NA,NA,Interrupt Status Verification,ISR,"GPIO IP out of reset. Group interrupt must be enabled for the target pin. Per-pin interrupt must be configured and triggered.","1. Configure a GPIO pin for level-triggered interrupt and enable its group interrupt.
2. Trigger the interrupt via external stimulus.
3. In the ISR, read the group interrupt status register.
4. Verify that the bit corresponding to the current pin (1<<pin) is set in the status register.
5. Clear the per-pin interrupt and disable the group enable.
6. Read the group status register again and verify it is 0x0.
7. Repeat for all 32 pins.",Group interrupt status register correctly reflects the interrupting pin bit and returns to 0x0 after interrupt clear and group disable.,"PASS: (rdata_grp & (1<<i)) != 0 when interrupt is active, and rdata_grp == 0x0 after clear. FAIL: Bit not set when expected, or status not cleared.",High,Interrupt Group Status Verification,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"The group interrupt status register is read-only and reflects the masked interrupt state of each pin."
14,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the per-pin interrupt clear mechanism. After an interrupt fires, writing 1 to the intr_clr field (bit 16) of the per-pin GPIO register should clear the interrupt raw status. The test writes 0x00110000 to clear the interrupt and then reads back the register expecting the value 0x100001.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c",gp0_gpio_8,0x0,32,"intr_clr; io_ctrl","16; 20","WO; RW2","0; 1","Interrupt clear (write-only); GPIO mode select",MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8,NA,NA,NA,Interrupt Clear Verification,ISR,"GPIO IP out of reset. Interrupt must have been raised on the target pin before clear can be tested.","1. After an interrupt fires on a GPIO pin, write 0x00110000 to the per-pin register to set the intr_clr bit and maintain io_ctrl in input mode.
2. Wait for the clear to take effect.
3. Read back the per-pin register.
4. Verify the read-back value equals 0x100001 (io_ctrl=1 in input mode, data_in=1, all interrupt bits cleared).
5. Report PASS if matched; FAIL otherwise.",Per-pin register reads 0x100001 after interrupt clear confirming interrupt raw status is cleared and GPIO remains in input mode.,"PASS: rdata == 0x100001 after writing 0x00110000 to clear interrupt. FAIL: rdata != 0x100001 (interrupt clear failed).",High,Interrupt Clear Mechanism,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"The intr_clr field is write-only (WO). Writing 1 clears the interrupt; writing 0 has no effect. The expected read-back value 0x100001 assumes io_ctrl=1 (bit 20) and data_in=1 (bit 0)."
15,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the sysreg-level interrupt status clear for GPIO0. After the GPIO interrupt is serviced, the test writes the GPIO0 interrupt bit to the sysreg raw_stcr1 register to clear the sysreg-level interrupt status, then reads back to confirm the bit is cleared.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c","raw_stcr1; intr_en1","0x24; 0x28",32,"gpio0_intr; gpio0_intr","1; 1","RAWSTCR1; INTREN1","0; 0","GPIO0 interrupt raw status/clear in sysreg; GPIO0 interrupt enable in sysreg","MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1",NA,NA,NA,Sysreg Interrupt Status Clear,ISR,"GPIO IP out of reset. Sysreg interrupt enable for GPIO0 must be set. GPIO interrupt must have been raised and serviced at the per-pin and group level before sysreg clear.","1. After servicing the GPIO interrupt at the per-pin and group level, write the GPIO0 interrupt bit to the sysreg raw status/clear register (raw_stcr1) to clear the sysreg-level interrupt.
2. Read back the sysreg raw status register.
3. Verify that the GPIO0 interrupt bit is cleared (bit value is 0).
4. Report PASS if cleared; FAIL otherwise.",Sysreg raw status register shows GPIO0 interrupt bit cleared after write to raw_stcr1.,"PASS: (rdata & gpio0_intr_bit) == 0 after writing clear bit to raw_stcr1. FAIL: GPIO0 interrupt bit still set in sysreg (sysreg status not cleared).",High,Sysreg Interrupt Clear Verification,GPIO0 instance,"This validates the full interrupt clear chain: per-pin clear -> group clear -> sysreg clear. The sysreg interrupt enable (intr_en1) must have been configured at test start."
16,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"This test verifies the external SRAM trigger mechanism used to stimulate GPIO interrupts. A write to the SRAM address 0xA0243ffc is used to drive GPIO pin levels and trigger level-sensitive interrupts. For active-high mode 0xFFFFFFFF is written; for active-low mode the inverted pin pattern ~(1<<i) is written.",GPIO,TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"program.c, test_define.c",NA,0xA0243ffc,NA,NA,NA,NA,NA,NA,0xA0243ffc,NA,NA,NA,External Stimulus Trigger,ISR,"SRAM address 0xA0243ffc must be accessible and mapped. GPIO pins must be configured in input mode before stimulus is applied.","1. For active-high testing: write 0xFFFFFFFF to the external SRAM trigger address to drive all GPIO pins high.
2. For active-low testing: write the inverted bit pattern ~(1<<pin) to drive the target pin low while others remain high.
3. Verify that the GPIO interrupt fires as expected after the SRAM write.
4. In the ISR, write 0xFFFFFFFF to the SRAM address to reset the stimulus.",GPIO interrupts are triggered by the SRAM write stimulus for both active-high and active-low configurations.,PASS: Interrupts fire correctly after SRAM stimulus write. FAIL: No interrupt generated after SRAM write (int_pend remains 1).,Medium,External Stimulus / Trigger Mechanism,GPIO pins 8-39 (all 32 pins),"The SRAM address 0xA0243ffc is not a GPIO register but an external memory-mapped location used to drive GPIO pin levels in the test environment. This address is not found in any register specification document."